    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48971" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tressis</span></b> , is, m.
		tres-as, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Three</i> asses, <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 5, § 169</span></i>; <i><span class="en">9, §
			81</span></i> Müll.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> To denote <i>a trifle</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hic Dama est non tressis agaso,</span>”
				<i>is not worth three coppers</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Pers.
					5, 76</span></i>
			.</div>
